import H0mework.Physics.LCDesign.EstimatedFrequency

/-!
# Executed-duration calibration with estimated frequency and disturbance

The run no longer executes the definitionally exact scheduled duration.  An
estimated-frequency calibration and a separately registered bound on the
actually executed accumulated phase generate the actual phase tolerance,
positive duration, linear-operator tolerance and existing ten-channel crown.

This is the mathematical clock/run mouth.  It does not assert that a physical
clock or instrument has already supplied the registered values.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

